# shell: desktop
# CW-001/AW-004, part one: a window is moved, and the session ends.  What it
# left behind is what session2.script starts from -- the two scripts are one
# test that a process boundary runs through.
note the window opens where the cascade put it
expect-window-at 45 40
note it is dragged somewhere deliberate
press 120 50
move 300 200
release 300 200
wait 5
expect-window-at 225 190
note the columns it is left with are remembered too: this shell called
note neither half of the pair, so every column change died with the window
expect-columns 4
note a second window, moved and CLOSED, is remembered by the close too --
note not only by the quit
click-row 0
click-row 0
wait 8
expect-title sub
note it opens cascaded, since its parent has no saved frame yet
expect-window-at 67 62
press 97 71
move 447 400
release 447 400
wait 5
expect-window-at 417 391
key w ctrl
wait 5
note re-opening it brings it back where it was closed
click-row 0
click-row 0
wait 8
expect-title sub
expect-window-at 417 391
quit
